Name: wakeWordDetected

Type: message

Syntax: wakeWordDetected

Summary:
Sent to the current card of the default stack when the speech recognition
engine detects the configured wake word. The command window is now open
and registered voice command phrases will be matched.

Introduced: 1.1.0

OS: mac

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Give audio feedback when the wake word is detected
on wakeWordDetected
    beep
end wakeWordDetected

Example:
-- Show a visual indicator
on wakeWordDetected
    show image "listeningIndicator"
end wakeWordDetected

on listenTimeoutExpired
    hide image "listeningIndicator"
end listenTimeoutExpired

on voiceCommand pPhrase
    hide image "listeningIndicator"
    -- handle pPhrase...
end voiceCommand

Description:
<wakeWordDetected> is dispatched immediately after the engine recognises
the wake word set with <setWakeWord>. After this message the engine
enters a command window during which it listens for registered phrases.
If a registered phrase is recognised within the timeout period,
<voiceCommand> is dispatched and the engine returns to waiting for the
wake word. If no phrase is recognised before the timeout,
<listenTimeoutExpired> is dispatched instead.

This message is only dispatched when a wake word has been set. When no
wake word is configured, the engine matches commands directly and
<wakeWordDetected> is never sent.

References: setWakeWord (command), listenTimeoutExpired (message),
voiceCommand (message), startListening (command)

Tags: speech, voice
